---
/**
 * /safety — hazing, conduct, and how to report a problem.
 *
 * WHAT THIS PAGE IS FOR
 * ---------------------
 * It is the page a worried parent is actually looking for. It works only if
 * it does not ask to be taken on trust, so almost everything on it points
 * *outside* the chapter: the state law, the university's policy and its
 * public record of hazing findings, the national fraternity's position, and
 * report lines the chapter does not control. The chapter's own statement is
 * one short section among them, not the whole page.
 *
 * ⚠️ DRAFT: the "Where we stand" section is a first draft written at the
 * owner's request (2026-09-28) and must be revised by the owner before the
 * domain goes live. It describes chapter conduct, which only the chapter can
 * vouch for. Keep it plain and humble; do not add claims the chapter cannot
 * stand behind if a parent asks.
 *
 * Every link here lives in chapter.json → safety, so an officer can update a
 * URL or phone number without touching this file. Do not add a named adult,
 * an advisor, or a house director until the owner supplies one.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CTAButton from '../components/CTAButton.astro';
import { chapter, isTodo } from '../lib/chapter';

const { safety, contact } = chapter;

const hasChapterEmail = !isTodo(contact.chapterEmail);
const hotlineHref = `tel:+1${safety.ouHotline.replace(/\D/g, '')}`;

/** The three bodies whose rules apply to the chapter, outermost first. */
const rules = [
  {
    name: 'Oklahoma law',
    body: 'Hazing is a crime in Oklahoma under Title 21, Section 1190 of the state statutes. The law applies to individual students as well as to the organizations they belong to.',
    href: safety.oklahomaStatute,
    linkLabel: 'Read the statute',
  },
  {
    name: 'The University of Oklahoma',
    body: 'OU prohibits hazing under its own hazing policy, which applies to every student organization on campus, and it investigates the reports it receives.',
    href: safety.ouPolicies,
    linkLabel: 'OU hazing laws and policies',
  },
  {
    name: 'Pi Kappa Phi',
    body: 'The national fraternity states that its Supreme Chapter and National Council "unequivocally oppose all acts of hazing." Its published statements of position also cover alcohol, drugs, and sexual misconduct.',
    href: safety.nationalPositions,
    linkLabel: 'Pi Kappa Phi statements of position',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Safety and conduct"
  description="Where the Alpha Gamma Chapter of Pi Kappa Phi stands on hazing, the rules it is held to, and how to report a problem without going through the chapter."
>
  <!-- ── Header ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 pb-14 pt-16 sm:px-8 sm:pt-24">
    <p class="font-mono text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-slate">
      Safety and conduct
    </p>

    <h1 class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-[2.5rem] leading-[1.08] sm:text-5xl">
      Hazing, safety, and how to report a problem
    </h1>

    <div class="mt-8 h-px w-24 bg-gold" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <p class="mt-8 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate">
      If you are a parent, this is probably the page you came for. Below is where the chapter
      stands, the rules we are held to by people other than ourselves, and how to report something
      without going through us at all.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Where we stand (DRAFT: owner to revise) ───────────────────── -->
  <section aria-labelledby="stance" class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 pb-20 sm:px-8">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,1.15fr)] lg:gap-16">
      <div>
        <p class="font-mono text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-gold-text">
          Our position
        </p>
        <h2 id="stance" class="mt-3 text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">Where we stand</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="border-l-2 border-gold pl-6 sm:pl-8">
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate sm:text-lg">
          Hazing has no place in joining this chapter. No one should be asked to do anything
          humiliating, dangerous, or illegal to become a member, and a bid never depends on it. The
          new member period is for learning the history of the fraternity and getting to know the
          people in it.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate sm:text-lg">
          If a new member is ever asked to do something that feels wrong, he can say no, and he can
          report it using any of the routes below. We would rather hear about a problem early, from
          anyone, than find out about it later. Raising a concern should never cost anyone their
          bid.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── The rules we are held to ──────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section aria-labelledby="rules" class="border-y-2 border-gold bg-paper">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
      <p class="font-mono text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-gold-text">
        Not our rules alone
      </p>
      <h2 id="rules" class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">
        The rules we are held to
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-slate">
        The chapter answers to three bodies outside itself. Each one publishes its own rules, so you
        can read them in the original rather than in our summary.
      </p>

      <ol class="mt-10 grid gap-px border border-ink/10 bg-ink/10 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {
          rules.map((rule) => (
            <li class="flex flex-col bg-paper p-6 sm:p-8">
              <h3 class="text-xl leading-snug">{rule.name}</h3>
              <p class="mt-3 flex-1 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-slate">{rule.body}</p>
              <a
                href={rule.href}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener"
                class="mt-5 inline-block py-1 text-[0.9375rem] text-royal underline underline-offset-4"
              >
                {rule.linkLabel}
                <span aria-hidden="true"> ↗</span>
                <span class="sr-only">(opens in a new tab)</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Check the record ──────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section aria-labelledby="record" class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
    <div class="border border-ink/10 p-6 sm:p-10">
      <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_auto] lg:items-center lg:gap-12">
        <div class="max-w-2xl">
          <p class="font-mono text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-gold-text">
            Public record
          </p>
          <h2 id="record" class="mt-3 text-2xl leading-snug sm:text-3xl">
            Check the record yourself
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate">
            Federal law now requires universities to publish every case in which a student
            organization was found responsible for hazing. OU's report names the organization,
            describes what happened, and gives the outcome. We would rather you read it than take
            our word for anything on this page.
          </p>
        </div>

        <CTAButton href={safety.ouTransparencyReport} variant="outline" external class="shrink-0">
          OU hazing transparency report
        </CTAButton>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── How to report ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section aria-labelledby="report" class="border-t border-ink/10 bg-ink text-paper">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
      <h2 id="report" class="max-w-2xl text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">
        How to report something
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-paper/70 sm:text-lg">
        You never have to go through the chapter to report a problem. Any of these routes works, and
        the first three are run by people outside it.
      </p>

      <dl class="mt-10 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-8 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="border-t border-paper/15 pt-5">
          <dt class="font-mono text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-gold">
            In an emergency
          </dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-paper/70">
            Call <a href="tel:911" class="text-paper underline underline-offset-4">911</a>. Do not
            wait to report it anywhere else first.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div class="border-t border-paper/15 pt-5">
          <dt class="font-mono text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-gold">
            To the university
          </dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-paper/70">
            OU takes reports through{' '}
            <a
              href={safety.ouReportForm}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
              class="text-paper underline underline-offset-4"
              >its online reporting page<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a
            >, and by phone on a line run by an independent company at{' '}
            <a href={hotlineHref} class="whitespace-nowrap text-paper underline underline-offset-4"
              >{safety.ouHotline}</a
            >.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div class="border-t border-paper/15 pt-5">
          <dt class="font-mono text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-gold">
            To the national fraternity
          </dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-paper/70">
            Pi Kappa Phi runs{' '}
            <a
              href={safety.nationalReport}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
              class="text-paper underline underline-offset-4"
              >an anonymous reporting line<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a
            >. The person reporting is not identified.
          </dd>
        </div>

        {
          hasChapterEmail && (
            <div class="border-t border-paper/15 pt-5">
              <dt class="font-mono text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-gold">
                To us
              </dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-paper/70">
                If you would rather start with the chapter, write to{' '}
                <a
                  href={`mailto:${contact.chapterEmail}`}
                  class="text-paper underline underline-offset-4 [overflow-wrap:anywhere]"
                >{contact.chapterEmail}</a>. You never have to.
              </dd>
            </div>
          )
        }
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
